 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Feature Handoff: voice-notes
     2	
     3	## Goal
     4	A macOS background daemon: hotkey to dictate a timestamped voice note (low-latency,
     5	high-accuracy STT), and a second hotkey to speak queries answered from the notes
     6	("show / today / search / summarize / ask") via Claude.
     7	
     8	## Files changed
     9	40 files, +3329 / -5 vs `main`. Highlights:
    10	- `src/instant_notes/stt/` — `base.py` (STTBackend + StreamingSession interfaces),
    11	  4 backends (`faster_whisper`, `sarvam`, `groq`, `deepgram`), `registry.py`.
    12	- `src/instant_notes/{audio,storage,config,intent,notify,hotkeys,daemon,cli}.py`.
    13	- `src/instant_notes/bench/` — WER + latency harness + report.
    14	- `tests/` — 6 test modules (39 passing, 1 gated skip).
    15	- `docs/adr/0001–0003`, `docs/features/voice-notes/design.md`, CI workflow.
    16	
    17	## How to run
    18	```bash
    19	python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
    20	pip install -e ".[all,dev]"        # all = faster-whisper + groq + deepgram SDKs
    21	cp .env.example .env               # fill SARVAM/GROQ/DEEPGRAM/ANTHROPIC keys
    22	instant-notes start                # daemon: Cmd+Shift+Space dictate, Cmd+Shift+A query
    23	instant-notes notes [--search Q] [--today]
    24	instant-notes bench --audio sample.wav --reference ref.txt
    25	```
    26	Tests/quality: `pytest -q`, `ruff check src tests`, `mypy`.
    27	
    28	## Expected behavior
    29	- Capture hotkey: toggle record → transcribe → save note (+ optional paste-at-cursor).
    30	- Command hotkey: toggle record → transcribe → intent-route → notify + print answer.
    31	- If the backend supports streaming (Deepgram live, faster-whisper windowed),
    32	  transcription runs *during* recording; otherwise batch on stop. Streaming
    33	  failures fall back to batch.
    34	- Retrieval intents (show/today/search) work offline with no API key; summarize/ask
    35	  use Claude and degrade gracefully without `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.
    36	
    37	## Test plan
    38	- **Automated (hermetic, mocked):** storage+FTS, intent routing (fake Claude),
    39	  cloud backends (mocked HTTP/SDK), bench WER/latency + error handling, CLI
    40	  (version/notes/bench-args), streaming (fake session + daemon path). 39 pass.
    41	- **Needs manual / real keys (not yet done):**
    42	  - End-to-end with a real mic + Microphone/Accessibility permissions.
    43	  - Real API calls per backend (no key in build env) — esp. Sarvam request shape
    44	    and Deepgram **live websocket event signatures**.
    45	  - The bench-off on a real voice sample (latency + WER comparison).
    46	
    47	## Known risks
    48	- **Deepgram streaming event handler** (`_DeepgramStreamingSession`) is coded to
    49	  the v3 SDK contract but unexercised against a live socket — the `is_final` /
    50	  `UtteranceEnd` shapes and handler signature could differ. First place to look
    51	  if streaming yields empty text.
    52	- **Sarvam** request shape (multipart + `language_code`) is unverified against the
    53	  live API; may need field tweaks on first real call.
    54	- **faster-whisper windowed streaming** re-transcribes the whole buffer every ~3s
    55	  (O(n²)); fine for short notes, revisit for long dictation (see ADR 0001).
    56	- Global hotkeys/paste need macOS Accessibility; mic needs Microphone permission.
    57	
    58	## Open questions
    59	- Final default backend — decide from the bench-off data.
    60	- Whisper model size default (`small`) — tune for the latency/accuracy target.
    61	- Spoken (TTS) responses — deferred; text-only for v1.

