     1	# Design: Instant Notes (voice-notes MVP)
     2	
     3	> Status: scoped 2026-06-08. Synthesized from user brief + clarifying answers.
     4	> Assumptions are marked **[ASSUMPTION]** — override any of these and I'll adjust.
     5	
     6	## 1. Goal
     7	
     8	A macOS background daemon that turns speech into notes instantly, with a
     9	Wispr-Flow-class latency/accuracy bar. Two interactions, both hotkey-driven:
    10	
    11	1. **Capture** — press hotkey to start recording, press again to stop. Audio is
    12	   transcribed and saved as a timestamped note.
    13	2. **Command/Query** — press a second hotkey, speak a request ("show my notes",
    14	   "summarize my notes", "what did I note today"). The spoken command is
    15	   transcribed, its intent is classified, and the app answers using the stored
    16	   notes + the Claude API.
    17	
    18	## 2. Non-negotiables
    19	
    20	- **Low latency.** Stop-talking → text-available must feel instant. We measure
    21	  it (see Benchmark) and optimize it across the 10–15 improvement loops.
    22	- **Accuracy.** Real transcription quality, measured as WER against a reference.
    23	- **Pluggable STT.** Four interchangeable backends behind one interface so we
    24	  can benchmark and swap the winner in.
    25	
    26	## 3. STT backends (the bench-off)
    27	
    28	| Backend           | Type   | Model                     | Needs key            | Streaming |
    29	|-------------------|--------|---------------------------|----------------------|-----------|
    30	| faster-whisper    | local  | configurable (e.g. `small`, `medium`, `large-v3`) | none | chunked |
    31	| Sarvam AI         | cloud  | `saarika` (Sarvam STT)    | `SARVAM_API_KEY`     | batch     |
    32	| Groq              | cloud  | `whisper-large-v3-turbo`  | `GROQ_API_KEY`       | batch (fast) |
    33	| Deepgram          | cloud  | `nova-3`                  | `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY`   | yes (websocket) |
    34	
    35	All four implement the same `STTBackend` interface and emit timing metrics so
    36	the benchmark is apples-to-apples.
    37	
    38	## 4. Architecture
    39	
    40	```
    41	hotkey press ─▶ AudioRecorder (sounddevice, 16kHz mono PCM)
    42	                     │ press again
    43	                     ▼
    44	              STTBackend.transcribe()  ──▶ TranscriptionResult{text, metrics}
    45	                     │
    46	        ┌────────────┴─────────────┐
    47	   capture mode                command mode
    48	        │                           │
    49	   NoteStore.add()           IntentRouter.route(text)
    50	   (SQLite + FTS5)                  │
    51	        │                  ┌────────┴─────────┐
    52	        ▼               show / today      summarize / ask
    53	   notify + log         NoteStore query   Claude API over notes
    54	                                              │
    55	                                          notify + print
    56	```
    57	
    58	### Modules (`src/instant_notes/`)
    59	- `cli.py` — entry point: `start` (daemon), `bench`, `notes`, `config`.
    60	- `daemon.py` — wires hotkeys → recorder → STT → router; long-running loop.
    61	- `hotkeys.py` — global hotkeys (`pynput`). Toggle-to-record. **[ASSUMPTION]**
    62	  capture = `Cmd+Shift+Space`, command = `Cmd+Shift+A` (configurable).
    63	- `audio.py` — record to in-memory buffer + optional WAV; resample to 16k mono.
    64	- `stt/base.py` — `STTBackend` ABC + `TranscriptionResult` + `STTMetrics`.
    65	- `stt/{faster_whisper,sarvam,groq,deepgram}_backend.py` — adapters.
    66	- `stt/registry.py` — name → backend factory; reads config/env.
    67	- `storage.py` — SQLite DAO. `notes(id, created_at, text, source_backend,
    68	  duration_ms, latency_ms, audio_path)`, FTS5 virtual table for search.
    69	- `intent.py` — classify spoken command → {show_recent, today, search,
    70	  summarize, ask}; fulfill using `storage` + Claude (`anthropic` SDK).
    71	- `notify.py` — macOS notification (`osascript`) + terminal output; optional
    72	  paste-at-cursor for capture results. **[ASSUMPTION]** paste-at-cursor OFF by
    73	  default (needs Accessibility perms); notes always saved.
    74	- `config.py` — load `config.toml` + `.env`; defaults + validation.
    75	- `bench/harness.py` — run N backends over a sample, collect metrics.
    76	- `bench/metrics.py` — WER (`jiwer`) + latency aggregation; markdown/JSON report.
    77	
    78	### Latency instrumentation
    79	Every transcription records: `record_stop_ts`, `request_sent_ts`,
    80	`first_token_ts` (streaming only), `final_ts`, `total_ms`. The benchmark and the
    81	live daemon both populate `STTMetrics` so we optimize against real numbers.
    82	
    83	## 5. Config & secrets
    84	- `.env` (gitignored): `SARVAM_API_KEY`, `GROQ_API_KEY`, `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY`,
    85	  `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. `.env.example` committed.
    86	- `config.toml`: hotkeys, `default_backend`, whisper model size, paste-at-cursor
    87	  toggle, intent-router model id. `config.example.toml` committed.
    88	
    89	## 6. LLM layer
    90	- Routing + summarize/ask via the `anthropic` SDK.
    91	  **[ASSUMPTION]** routing uses `claude-haiku-4-5` (cheap/fast), summarize/ask
    92	  uses `claude-opus-4-8`. Configurable.
    93	
    94	## 7. Testing
    95	- `pytest`. Unit: storage CRUD + FTS, intent classification (Claude mocked),
    96	  backend interface conformance (HTTP mocked for cloud, tiny local model gated
    97	  behind a marker). Bench metrics: WER + latency math on fixtures.
    98	
